  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Uncovering circuit mechanisms of current sinks and sources with biophysical simulations of primary visual cortex (2022) in Dryad. 38 download(s) recorded.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Uncovering circuit mechanisms of current sinks and sources with biophysical simulations of primary visual cortex (2022) in Dryad is authored by Rimehaug, Atle, Stasik, Alexander and Hagen, Espen. Topics: Neuroscience, Visual cortex, Local field potential, Computer science and Current (fluid).</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">No citations yet.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Limited online visibility beyond citations.</p>",
  "provenance": {},
  "story_type": "DataStory",
  "publisher": "Dryad",
  "narrative_llm": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This Dryad dataset shows early signs of use and reuse in the research record: 38 downloads, 361 views, and two documented downstream reuse events. It has not yet accumulated OpenAlex citations, so the clearest evidence of impact today is in access and reuse rather than citation volume.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This dataset supports a biophysical investigation of current sinks and sources in mouse primary visual cortex, pairing public Neuropixels recordings with a detailed circuit model. The record places it in neuroscience and visual-cortex research, with the underlying work spanning synaptic, cellular, and circuit-level analysis of local field potential and current source density signals.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The strongest impact signal is reuse: the dataset has two documented downstream reuses in biomedical articles, and one journal article is explicitly registered as citing the dataset as a supplemental resource. That pattern suggests the data are being incorporated into follow-on work, even though the citation count in OpenAlex remains at zero.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Usage data also show a modest but real audience: 361 views and 38 downloads. Combined with the open-access Dryad repository context and the linked derived analysis code, the record indicates that the dataset is accessible and has already been taken up by readers and secondary users, though on a limited scale so far.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The broader attention record is still sparse. There are no indexed online mentions in the available event-data sources, and scite reports no citation statements captured for this item. In other words, the dataset\u2019s present footprint is defined more by direct access and a small number of documented reuses than by wider public discussion or citation accumulation.</p>",
  "narrative_source": "template"
